    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 268 of 1989",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8370\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend chapter 268 of the laws of 1989 amending the vehicle and\ntraffic law relating to providing for payment of fees and other charges\nby credit card, in relation to the effectiveness of such provisions\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo extend the provisions in the Vehicle and Traffic Law relating to\npayment of motor vehicle fees by credit card.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nThe bill amends Chapter 268 of the Laws of 1989 in order to extend until\nJuly 7, 2014 the statute authorizing the Department of Motor Vehicles\n(DMV) to accept payment by credit Card.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nSection 202-a of the Vehicle and Traffic Law authorizes the New York\nState Department of Motor Vehicles to establish a system by which motor\nvehicle-related fees, fines, etc. can be paid by credit card. This\nsystem has proven an important tool to enhance the department's effi-\nciency, effectiveness, customer service and convenience.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2006: A.10139 (Gantt) - Passed both Houses;\nSigned Chapter 145 of the Laws of 2006.\n2002: A.11373 (Gantt) - Passed both Houses; Signed Chapter 108 of the\nLaws of 2002.\n1998: A.10423 (Tokasz) - Passed both Houses; Signed Chapter 129 of\nthe Laws of 1998.\n1996: A.10999 (Rules/Gantt) Passed both Houses; Signed Chapter 280 of\nthe Laws of 1996.\n1993 A.7174-B (Bragmann) - Passed both Houses; Signed Chapter 558 of\nthe Laws of 1993.\n1991: A.7458 (Bragmann) - Passed both Houses; Signed Chapter 134 of\nthe Laws of 1991.\n1989: A.7110-A (Tokasz) - Passed both Houses; Signed Chapter 268 of\nthe Laws of 1989.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\nUnknown.\n\nEFFECTIVE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
